<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 21:22:10 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo arrives in Uruguay for first stop on 12-day South America tour</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-pope-leo-arrives-in-uruguay-for-first-stop-on-12-day-south-america-tour</link><description>
Pope Leo touched down in Uruguay on Friday to begin a 12-day tour of South America that will also see him visit Argentina and Peru. The tour is seen as something of a homecoming for the pontiff who lived in Peru for almost two decades and holds joint US and Peruvian citizenship.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aab0508-da1a-11f1-81c8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-06T193927Z-1437835472-RC2JIOACA4EZ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aab0508-da1a-11f1-81c8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-06T193927Z-1437835472-RC2JIOACA4EZ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3283e0f4-da24-11f1-a6d8-95d5f1845f91</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 21:14:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aab0508-da1a-11f1-81c8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-06T193927Z-1437835472-RC2JIOACA4EZ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump announces immigration hardliner Stephen Miller as new chief of staff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-announces-immigration-hardliner-stephen-miller-as-new-chief-of-staff</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Friday said advisor Stephen Miller would become his new chief of staff. Miller has been instrumental in driving the Trump administration's mass deportation programme and faced particular criticism after the deadly shootings of two Minneapolis protesters by ICE agents in January.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4ccbd52-da20-11f1-92bf-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6PN3T3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4ccbd52-da20-11f1-92bf-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6PN3T3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac163ece-da21-11f1-a81a-0383cf3d852d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 20:51:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4ccbd52-da20-11f1-92bf-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6PN3T3.jpg">© Chip Somodevilla, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The World This Week</category><title>Midterms: A Maga PostMortem, Europe’s ‘Shape Shifting’ Protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261106-midterms-a-maga-postmortem-europe-s-shape-shifting-protests</link><description>
A World This Week ‘Mid Terms Special’ 
 
Gavin Lee is joined by panel of four distinguished international correspondents to assess the aftermath of the worst Republican election result since the 1970s, post Watergate. We ask, is peak MAGA over? What will now change at home and abroad? And who ends the week in pole position as Presidential frontrunner for 2028?
 
We also consider the scale and scope of Europe Wide Protests:  
 
This week housing organisations, trade unions and activist groups from seven countries met in Paris issuing a joint call for demonstrations. Are the national protest movements becoming a coordinated European movement?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e82e01f4-da1b-11f1-b402-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/81f9ea5b-a81b-4236-b01d-3d25e74ea1f6.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e82e01f4-da1b-11f1-b402-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/81f9ea5b-a81b-4236-b01d-3d25e74ea1f6.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7761de0-da1d-11f1-8391-1b8f54bdb46f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 20:08:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Alessandro XENOS</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>A homegrown Georgia moderate and pragmatist: Is Senator Ossoff the future of the Democratic Party?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261106-a-homegrown-georgia-moderate-and-pragmatist-is-senator-ossoff-the-future-of-the-democratic-party</link><description>
Is Senator Jon Ossoff the future of the Democratic Party? Following a resounding midterm victory in Georgia, a former Republican stronghold, the 39-year-old senator has emerged as a prominent figure as the Democrats look ahead to 2028 for their next presidential nominee. His natural confidence, polished media performances and ability to appeal to a diverse electorate have prompted comparisons with Barack Obama. Yet behind the excitement surrounding his national prospects lies a more complicated question: whether political momentum in the Senate necessarily translates into a presidential frontrunner.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b07c7ea8-da0b-11f1-ba8e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-181104-182336-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b07c7ea8-da0b-11f1-ba8e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-181104-182336-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2bf03f84-da1b-11f1-b582-41f7c3676cec</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 19:49:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>US midterms mark 'the beginning of the end' for Trump, John Bolton says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261106-us-midterms-mark-the-beginning-of-the-end-for-trump-john-bolton-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, John Bolton, who served as national security adviser to Donald Trump during his first term, called the US midterm results "the beginning of the end" for Trump's stranglehold on the Republican Party. Democrats regained control of both the House of Representatives and the Senate earlier this week, marking the Republicans' worst performance since the 1974 elections in the wake of the Watergate scandal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/329cac82-da02-11f1-8c02-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-john-bolton.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/329cac82-da02-11f1-8c02-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-john-bolton.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce3e0d66-d9f8-11f1-8676-4f5175760546</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 17:26:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope Leo embarks on Latin America trip with a first stop in Uruguay</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-pope-leo-embarks-on-latin-america-trip-with-a-first-stop-in-uruguay</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV is kicking off a three-nation tour of Latin America on Friday, November 6, with a visit to Uruguay, the region’s least Catholic and most secular country, three weeks after undergoing lung cancer surgery that had put the entire trip into question. After Uruguay, he will then go to Argentina and Peru. FRANCE 24's Hanna Roberts has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1dde444-d9ec-11f1-875a-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15e9c5b9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1dde444-d9ec-11f1-875a-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15e9c5b9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5bee38e6-d9ec-11f1-b58a-d3ec7f982f66</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 14:58:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>California governor to grant clemency to all 548 death row inmates in state</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-california-governor-to-grant-clemency-to-all-548-death-row-inmates-in-state</link><description>
California's governor Gavy Newsom announced Thursday that he will commute all death sentences in the state to life without the possibility of parole. He said that "capital punishment is morally wrong." The state Supreme Court will have the final say in hundreds of those cases.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06d29b9a-d9ec-11f1-b5f2-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-77fd1be3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06d29b9a-d9ec-11f1-b5f2-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-77fd1be3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7555a644-d9eb-11f1-b34b-9de4add3b6a8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 14:54:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>The women who rode the blue wave</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261106-the-women-who-rode-the-blue-wave</link><description>
In this edition, we report on how the US midterms, which saw the Democrats make massive gains, also marked a series of historic firsts for women. Also the dark side to Bangkok's booming fertility industry, which attracts thousands of foreign patients seeking assistance from the Thai capital's state-of-the-art private clinics. Plus how an impoverished neighbourhood in El Salvador, once a no-go zone plagued by gang violence, is being transformed by women into a vibrant canvas for street art.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f4db7a4-d9d7-11f1-b5a5-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f4db7a4-d9d7-11f1-b5a5-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7cd75936-d922-11f1-86b5-ef0b033d2e60</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 14:15:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump’s stillborn diesel deal: Why Russian oil tankers are not heading to the US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-stillborn-diesel-deal-why-russian-oil-tankers-are-not-heading-to-the-us</link><description>
The first oil tankers scheduled to deliver Russian diesel to the US under a deal between President Donald Trump and his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin have changed course and are no longer heading toward the US coast. It spells the end of an agreement announced with great fanfare before the midterms.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/583fe45e-d93a-11f1-9d4e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/image-tanker-diesel3.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/583fe45e-d93a-11f1-9d4e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/image-tanker-diesel3.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72572b5c-d9d7-11f1-aa8a-15a9cc0740e7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:38:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/583fe45e-d93a-11f1-9d4e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/image-tanker-diesel3.png">© Studio graphique France Médias Monde</source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth's future in question after midterms setback</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-us-defence-secretary-pete-hegseth-s-future-in-question-after-midterms-setback</link><description>
US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth's future is in question after Tuesday's, November 3, midterms setback. On Thursday, November 5, he issued a video message vowing to fight efforts in Congress to impeach him and defending the ‌Iran war as “courageous and historic”. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/786ab9d8-d9d6-11f1-88c5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bcc8d7a2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/786ab9d8-d9d6-11f1-88c5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bcc8d7a2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee8dbbc0-d9d5-11f1-bdf5-e56d28bb9ded</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:15:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tech giants lose $1 trillion in one day after Democrats victory in midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-tech-giants-lose-1-trillion-in-one-day-after-democrats-victory-in-midterms</link><description>
Trillions of dollars have been wiped off the stock value of major tech firms in the US, Europe and Asia. Investors appear worried about the possibility of an AI slowdown and tougher regulation as Democrats won the midterms in the US. Some of the Democratic candidates had expressed their opposition to the data centres that are needed to power AI technology.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e1d77ee-d9dc-11f1-9d72-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f9220cf.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e1d77ee-d9dc-11f1-9d72-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f9220cf.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d57022c-d9dc-11f1-817e-cfc74dac3b1b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:15:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Canada PM Mark Carney unveils budget to strengthen economy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-canada-pm-mark-carney-unveils-budget-to-strengthen-economy</link><description>
Canada's Prime Minister Mark Carney unveiled his first ever budget on November 5, which set out strong ambitions for greater economic independence from the US. The "Masters of our Destiny" budget also announced generous measures for parts of the economy affected by tariffs, setting aside 44 billion Canadian dollars for impacted businesses and workers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56f49bae-d9de-11f1-9e2c-cd4b49fae717</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:10:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Will Democratic Party introduce a new 'New Deal'? Key narrative must be 'focused on economic issues'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/will-democratic-party-introduce-a-new-new-deal-key-narrative-must-be-focused-on-economic-issues</link><description>
With Democrats poised to control both chambers of Congress, the party faces a defining challenge: how to constrain Donald Trump's presidency while carving out a path to the White House in 2028. For Ian Reifowitz, Distinguished Professor of History at SUNY Empire State University, the answer lies in drawing on the historical legacy of Franklin D. Roosevelt's New Deal coalition. Republicans, he argues, have progressively shifted electoral competition towards questions of identity, immigration and cultural conflict. Democrats, by contrast, must recover their traditional strength on economic security, affordability and everyday living standards. "These Democrats across the country ran on affordability." And that's how they must govern, explains Reifowitz.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d72ef50a-d9dc-11f1-96ab-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261105-223101-224205-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d72ef50a-d9dc-11f1-96ab-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261105-223101-224205-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dc7309f2-d9dc-11f1-ba9c-9776752ee81a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:07:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Period of uncertainty: Trump is tormented, he's unstoppable, and he's desperate for immortality'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261106-period-of-uncertainty-trump-is-tormented-he-s-unstoppable-and-he-s-desperate-for-immortality</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Craig Copetas, Greek-American author, international affairs columnist and editor at Türkiye Today and French Senator Hélène Conway-Mouret. "What you have is a tormented and unstable president who's desperate for immortality." With this arresting assessment, Copetas captures what he considers the defining paradox of Donald Trump's presidency in the aftermath of the US midterm elections: a leader politically neutered at home but potentially emboldened on the international stage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87cc9f50-da11-11f1-9afb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-abe726d1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87cc9f50-da11-11f1-9afb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-abe726d1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0cb298f0-d9e0-11f1-ae27-6156df5d338f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:46:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>California governor says commuting all death sentences in state</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-california-governor-says-commuting-all-death-sentences-in-state</link><description>
California Governor Gavin Newsom said Thursday, November 5, he was commuting all death sentences across the state to life imprisonment, in a move that will affect over 500 prisoners. FRANCE 24's correspondent Wassim Cornet reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0fd78a96-d9c6-11f1-b5f2-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-61e1f7e1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0fd78a96-d9c6-11f1-b5f2-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-61e1f7e1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac44f4fa-d9c5-11f1-92d2-d3bed1e9c4d4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:05:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>European stocks plunge after US midterm election results shock markets</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-live-european-stocks-plunge-after-us-midterm-election-results-shock-markets</link><description>
European shares tumbled on Friday as global investors grappled with uncertainty over AI stocks, following the Democrats’ sweeping victory in the US midterm elections. The drop was partly due to fears that Democrats could curb the development of AI data centres, which are widely unpopular among US voters. Read our liveblog to see how events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d71b2db8-d9be-11f1-82d6-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T161457Z-54596775-RC2QHOA0MWI0-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-STOCKS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d71b2db8-d9be-11f1-82d6-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T161457Z-54596775-RC2QHOA0MWI0-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-STOCKS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8a703baa-d9c0-11f1-9f11-6bfb823454de</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 09:37:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d71b2db8-d9be-11f1-82d6-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T161457Z-54596775-RC2QHOA0MWI0-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-STOCKS.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump calls midterms 'crooked', demands Alaska votes go to Republican candidate</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-calls-midterms-crooked-demands-alaska-votes-go-to-republican-candidate</link><description>
Despite having previously accepted the US midterm election results, President Donald Trump told reporters on Thursday the elections were "crooked", and he demanded the remaining votes for Alaska go to its incumbent Republican senator. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2183d514-d9b8-11f1-9fd9-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T213905Z-1662772902-RC2XHOA9PTOM-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2183d514-d9b8-11f1-9fd9-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T213905Z-1662772902-RC2XHOA9PTOM-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eff00dc4-d9b7-11f1-9b14-3f8ae2419849</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 08:20:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2183d514-d9b8-11f1-9fd9-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T213905Z-1662772902-RC2XHOA9PTOM-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg">© Elizabeth Frantz, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA['Leaders all over the world understand that Trump is only there for two more years & then he's gone']]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261106-leaders-all-over-the-world-understand-that-trump-is-only-there-for-two-more-years-then-he-s-gone</link><description>
In American politics, even presidential power has its limits. And now, the laws of political gravity may finally be catching up with Donald Trump's hyper-aggressive exercise of executive authority. Following what political scientist Ian Bremmer describes as the most consequential electoral reversal for a governing party in more than half a century, the president and founder of Eurasia Group and GZERO Media argues that the United States has entered a new political phase: the beginning of the end of Trump's ability to dominate the political agenda, at home and on the world stage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3110575c-d9d9-11f1-a7df-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1256966e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3110575c-d9d9-11f1-a7df-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1256966e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e9a20726-d9b0-11f1-91a4-6be270ac3682</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 07:08:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Rubio denies plans to resign, says working for Trump until end of term has 'always been my plan'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-marco-rubio-denies-resignation-2028-white-house</link><description>
